From 8d527341ee105dc3dde29ea4bb8af33fab7d6d59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mechanyaa-ai <mechanyaa@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:12:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cps2w: the vsavjw catalogue entry re-pointed to merged-m24
 (14z-216)

jtframe's .rom builder locates every zip member by CRC32 and by nothing else
(mra2rom.go:163-172, no name fallback), so the machine entry must name the
CRCs of the actual build or the MRA produces no .rom at all. Regenerated from
build/m3b_merged32/rompath/vsavjw.zip by tools/gen_vsavjw_xml.py in the
consuming tree; --check now reports the catalogue matches the build.

EIGHT members moved, and they are the M24 member delta exactly (the consuming
tree's build/agent216/m24/member_delta.txt):
  vm3j.03d  51a90934 -> 37c76a62   program: (M)'s palette-reload mask word
                                   (0x02ADB4) and #294's per-frame table row
                                   0x13 (0x02AE12) and dead-span jump
                                   (0x024024); pointers into placed space
                                   relocated by #294's allocations
  vm3j.04d  ef5acffb -> 21a3cfc1   program: pointer rows into placed space,
                                   relocated
  vm3j.07b  548977d5 -> da600dff   likewise
  vm3j.10b  49fdef4d -> 6330edd6   likewise
  vsw.41    21e69247 -> 3b66ac7e   wide extension: #294's routine and records,
                                   and the placed regions after them, moved
  vsw.42    bb7d6f89 -> bd9e86ff   likewise
  vsw.33m   cd4c6970 -> 87fe1e0c   group-C glyphs, the M23 -> M24 mark
  vsw.37m   9a136ffb -> 771c5dd9   likewise

No RTL, no cfg, no core change: doc/mame.xml only. cores/cps1, cores/cps2 and
cores/cps15 remain byte-untouched.
